What is it?
-----------

SafeCracker V1.1 [20-FEB-1999] PostCard Ware.
In the game of Safe Craker you job is to crack open a 3 dial safe.
You must find the right number for each dial and do it within 4 tries.
The safe numbers range from 1 to 100 and the lights below each dial
will inform you if you need to go higher > or lower <. Also, you are
able to get an idea of how far you need to go in the given direction.
It will not be the exact number but a close proxy. If you can set all
four dials without setting off an alarm, you will be able to open the
safe and claim the rewards inside.

It will cost you a given number of file or byte credits or Online Time
or Game Ponts to play and if you fail to open the safe, those are added
to the safe for the next person to take a shot at. If the game is set to
play for fake cash only, then it will not cost you anything to play.

As always, Use at your own risk. It works great here but may bomb
elsewhere.

Installation:
-------------

Read History.Doc for past version notes.

1. Unarch the program :) Lets hope this part is already done.
2. Move the SafeCrack directory to PFiles/doors (or anywhere). This program
   uses smart paths so it can always find it's needed files but you do
   need to keep the directory.
3. Add this line to your sys.welcome file or as a pfile/door:
   {#0Doors:SafeCrack/SafeCrack}
   ^
   Remember that the { is a CTRL-Q character
4. Set the configuration in the game to your needs.
5. Save any files you changed and if added to bbsmenu also do a reload.

Thats it! Simple.

Configuration:
--------------

There are four (4) configuration options at the start of the code. These
maybe set to your needs. Since there are only 4 small options in this code
I opted no not code a seperate config program for time/speed sake :) The
text below will explane them in more detail.

cfg=1    This setting controls what your users will be playing for. If it's
         set to 0, they just play for fake cash and it costs them nothing to
         play the game. If set to 1 they will be playing for Byte Credits, 2
         File Credits, 3 Online Time and 4 for Door/Game points.

bet=1000 This setting is for how much of the users credits will be needed
         to play the game and what is added to the safe each time a user
         looses. If they do not have enough, the game will inform them and
         exit. If cfg is set for fake cash, this option only controls how
         much is added to the safe and costs the user nothing.

pot=1000 This option only sets the starting amount the safe will have after
         a user wins.

max=0    This option is not used in this version at this time.

ers=5    This option setting controls how far off the guess is when
         informing the user about their guess. The smaller the number the
         closer to the real number will be told. It's vary hard to guess a
         number from 1 to 100 in only 4 try's let alone 3 times in a row.
         The best results range from 5 to 10. Less than 5 and the game
         becomes too easy and more than 10 becomes too hard again.

